Q: Is there a way to call a function when a SwiftUI Picker selection changes? A: <p>There is now a cleaner way to accomplish this which leverages the selection binding property of <code>Picker</code>.</p>
<pre><code>enum Frequency: String, CaseIterable, Identifiable {
    case daily
    case hourly
    case weekly
    case monthly
    var id: Self { return self }

    var title: String {
        switch self {
            case .daily:
                return &quot;Daily&quot;
            case .hourly:
                return &quot;Hourly&quot;
            case .weekly:
               return &quot;Weekly&quot;
            case .monthly:
               return &quot;Monthly&quot;
        }
    }
}

struct FrequencyView: View {
    @State private var selectedFrequency = Frequency.daily

    var body: some View {
        Menu {
            Picker(&quot;Frequency&quot;, selection: $selectedFrequency) {
                ForEach(Frequency.allCases) {
                    Text($0.title)
                }
            }
            .onChange(of: selectedFrequency) { _ in
                myCoolFunction()
            }
        } label: {
            Text(selectedFrequency.title)
        }
    }

    private func myCoolFunction() {
        print(&quot;A cool function was called!&quot;)
    }
}
</code></pre>

Q: Use Microsoft Graph 5.0 SDK to get display name from listitem&#39;s LookupId field A: <p>Yes, you need to get a list of all users to find out the user associated with the <code>LookupId</code>.</p>
<p>The <strong>User Information List</strong> is a system list of all users.</p>
<p>To be able to list system lists, you need to specify <code>system</code> in the <code>$select</code> query parameter. Filter the list by the <code>displayName</code> if you want, but be aware the name of the <strong>User Information List</strong> can have a translation according to the set language.</p>
<pre><code>var result = await graphClient
                .Sites[&quot;{site-id}&quot;]
                .Lists
                .GetAsync((requestConfiguration) =&gt;
{
    requestConfiguration.QueryParameters.Select = new string []{ &quot;id&quot;,&quot;displayName&quot;,&quot;description&quot;,&quot;system&quot; };
    requestConfiguration.QueryParameters.Filter = &quot;displayName eq 'User Information List'&quot;;
});
</code></pre>
<p>Then use the id of the <strong>User Information List</strong> list and lookup id (ApproverLookupId in your case) to get details about the user.</p>
<pre><code>var result = await graphClient
                 .Sites[&quot;{site-id}&quot;]
                 .Lists[&quot;{UserInformationListId}&quot;]
                 .Items[&quot;{ApproverLookupId}&quot;]
                 .Fields
                 .GetAsync();
</code></pre>
